<title>PERU: Peru's bank liquidity rises 24 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>Peru's bank liquidity rises 24 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's total banking system liquidity rose to 31.498 billion soles at the end of 1996, 24 percent higher in real terms than the previous year, the Central Reserve Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>The figure was 39 percent higher in nominal terms than the total liquidity of 22.633 billion soles at the end of 1995, according to the bank's weekly report.</p>
<p>-- Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
